    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Here is one row from a leads spreadsheet. Some fields are already filled in, others are blank. Your job is to fill in every blank field you can, using the fewest tool calls necessary — don't call a tool for data that's already present, and don't call a tool if you have no way to get its required input yet.\n\nCurrent row data:\nfull_name: {{ $json.full_name }}\ncompany_name: {{ $json.company_name }}\nlinkedin_url: {{ $json.linkedin_url }}\nemail: {{ $json.email }}\ntitle: {{ $json.job }}\ndomain: {{ $json.domain }}\nwebsite: {{ $json.website }}\nphone: {{ $json.phone }}\nabout: {{ $json.about }}\nlocation: {{ $json.location }}\ncompany_linkedin: {{ $json.company_linkedin }}\n\nDependency logic to follow (a waterfall — use whichever entry point the row's existing data allows):\n- If linkedin_url is missing but email is present: use Reverse Email to LinkedIn URL to get it.\n- If linkedin_url is missing but full_name + company_name are present: use Find Person's LinkedIn URL instead.\n- Once you have a linkedin_url: use Get Full LinkedIn Profile Info to scrape the profile (this always returns a pending job — poll it to completion with Check Job Status, waiting between checks with the Wait 60 Seconds tool if needed). From that scrape, extract every one of these fields if present: full name, current job title, current company name, location, headline, about/summary, email, and phone number.\n- Regardless of whether the scrape included an email: always also call Find Person's Email to confirm or find the email if it's still missing.\n- Regardless of whether the scrape included a phone number: always also call Find Person's Phone to confirm or find the phone number if it's still missing.\n- If company_name is present but website/domain is missing: use Find Company Website.\n- If domain is now known: also use Find Company Employee Count and Find Company LinkedIn URL (company_linkedin) to round out company-level data.\n\nReturn the fully filled-in record with these exact fields: full_name, title, company_name, domain, website, linkedin_url, location, headline, about, email, phone, company_employee_count, company_linkedin. For any field you genuinely cannot find after trying the relevant tool, leave it as an empty string — never invent data.",
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "You are a data enrichment agent. Given a partial spreadsheet row, you dynamically decide which LinkFinder AI tools to call, in what order, based on what data is already present — not a fixed script. Be efficient: every tool call costs 1 credit even on a miss, so don't call a tool whose required input is missing, and don't re-fetch data that's already there. Never fabricate names, titles, emails, or any other field — leave genuinely unfindable fields blank."
        }
      },
      "id": "0d2d7e9e-5abf-4305-a4e6-4710b27dc6e5",
